.TH AIR 1 "August 2026" "AIR 0.1" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
air \- review commits with a local AI coding harness
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B air
.I COMMAND
.RI [ OPTIONS ]
.br
.B air help
.RI [ COMMAND
.RI [ SUBCOMMAND ]]
.br
.B air
.RB [ \-h | \-\-help ]
.br
.B air
.B \-\-version
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B AIR
is a local semantic reviewer for commits on the first-parent history of
.BR master .
It starts a fresh Codex, Claude Code, or Gemini CLI session for each selected
commit, lets that harness inspect the repository under a read-only policy, and
stores the resulting reviews and findings in a repository-specific SQLite
database.
.PP
AIR processes commits independently and supports both continuous and disjoint
review ranges. It does not check out historical commits. The selected harness
inspects each requested commit and any related repository context through its
own local tools.
.PP
Binary-only and empty diffs, and textual diffs larger than 256 KiB, are
recorded as skipped. Previously reviewed or skipped commits are not processed
again unless explicitly rescanned. Failed reviews enter a durable failure
queue and are deferred by later ordinary scans until
.B air retry
is run.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-h , " " \-\-help
Show global, command, or subcommand help. Long options may appear before or
after positional arguments. Use
.B \-\-
to stop option parsing when a positional value starts with a hyphen.
.TP
.B \-\-version
Print
.B air 0.1
and exit. This is equivalent to
.BR "air version" .
.SH COMMANDS
.SS Getting started
.TP
.BI "air init " COMMIT
Initialize AIR with
.I COMMIT
as the baseline. The baseline must occur on the first-parent history of local
.B master
and is not itself reviewed.
.TP
.BR "air doctor" " [\-\-json]"
Check the Git repository, master ref, state permissions, database schema and
integrity, effective review configuration, model pricing, selected harness
executable, and authentication where the harness exposes a noninteractive
check. Write a stable JSON report with
.BR \-\-json .
.TP
.BR "air status" " [\-\-json]"
Summarize total, open, dismissed, and resolved findings, as well as unscanned,
failed, and deferred commits. Estimate the remaining ordinary scan time from
successful timed commit reviews. Deferred failures are excluded from the
estimate.
.TP
.B air version
Print
.B air 0.1
and exit. This command does not require a Git repository or initialized AIR
state.
.SS Commit review
.TP
.BR "air pending" " [\-\-limit " N "] [" FROM .. TO "]"
List the commits an equivalent scan would process, without constructing a
reviewer or modifying AIR state. A zero limit means unlimited.
.TP
.BR "air scan" " [" OPTIONS "] [" FROM .. TO "]"
Review unprocessed commits after the baseline through local master, oldest
first. An explicit range excludes
.I FROM
and includes
.IR TO ;
both endpoints must occur on master's first-parent history.
.RS
.TP
.BI "\-\-limit " N
Process at most
.I N
commits. Zero, the default, means unlimited. The limit includes commits AIR
records as skipped.
.TP
.B \-\-dry-run
Show pending work without invoking a harness or writing state.
.TP
.B \-\-stop-on-error
Stop after recording the first failed commit. By default, AIR continues with
later commits and returns a failure after the batch.
.TP
.B "Review options"
The common review options described under
.B REVIEW OPTIONS
are also accepted.
.RE
.TP
.BR "air precheck" " [" OPTIONS "] [" FROM .. TO "]"
Review commits on local master that are not in its configured upstream, oldest
first, without modifying AIR state. An explicit first-parent range may be
supplied instead. New findings and predicted resolutions are provisional, and
only findings still open after the complete series are reported.
.RS
.TP
.B \-\-staged
Review the exact staged Git index against HEAD instead of reviewing commits.
HEAD must be the tip of local master. This option cannot be combined with a
commit range; unstaged and untracked changes are ignored.
.TP
.BI "\-\-format " FORMAT
Write
.BR text ,
.BR json ,
.BR sarif ,
or
.BR html .
The default is
.BR text .
.TP
.BI "\-o, \-\-output " FILE
Write the report directly to
.I FILE
instead of standard output. Use
.B -
for standard output.
.TP
.BI "\-\-fail-on " SEVERITY
Return a nonzero status when an outstanding provisional finding is at or above
.BR info ,
.BR warning ,
or
.BR error .
Without this option, findings do not change the exit status.
.TP
.B "Review options"
The common review options are also accepted and apply to each target.
.RE
.TP
.BR "air retry" " [" OPTIONS "]"
Retry live commits in the durable failure queue, oldest failure first, using
the current review configuration.
.RS
.TP
.BI "\-\-limit " N
Retry at most
.I N
commits. Zero means unlimited.
.TP
.B \-\-continue-on-error
Continue after recording another failed attempt. The default is to stop on
the first retry failure.
.TP
.B "Review options"
The common review options are also accepted.
.RE
.TP
.BR "air failures" " [\-\-json]"
List the durable failure queue. Each entry includes the latest error, attempt
count, timestamp, reviewer identity, and whether it was a rescan.
.TP
.BI "air rescan [" OPTIONS "] " COMMIT
Review one already processed commit again. The latest successful result
becomes current, while earlier review attempts and their accounting remain
available. The common review options are accepted.
.TP
.BI "air skip [\-\-reason " TEXT "] [\-\-dry-run] " COMMIT
Mark one unprocessed commit as skipped.
.TP
.BI "air skip \-\-filter " TEXT " [\-\-reason " TEXT "] [\-\-dry-run]"
Mark every unprocessed commit whose full commit message contains the literal
.I TEXT
substring, matched case-insensitively, as skipped. The default reason is
"manual skip". Selection is limited to commits after the baseline on master's
first-parent history. A bulk skip is atomic; skipping a failed commit removes
it from the retry queue.
.TP
.BR "air clean" " [\-\-dry-run]"
Remove processed-commit and failure records for commits no longer on master's
first-parent history. Use
.B \-\-dry-run
to preview stale records.
.SS Finding review
.TP
.BR "air recheck" " [" OPTIONS "] [" FINDING_ID " ...]"
Ask the configured harness whether selected open findings are resolved in the
exact current HEAD snapshot. With no IDs, recheck every eligible open finding.
HEAD must be the tip of master.
.RS
.TP
.BI "\-\-limit " N
Recheck at most
.I N
findings. Zero means unlimited.
.TP
.BI "\-\-batch-by " MODE
Group findings by
.B file
(the default) or
.BR count .
File mode batches each recorded file separately, in path order, splitting it
as needed to respect the batch-size cap. Findings without a file are batched
separately at the end. Count mode fills batches in selection order across files.
Grouping does not restrict which related files the reviewer may inspect.
.TP
.BI "\-\-batch-size " N
Send at most
.I N
findings per model call. The default is 20 and the maximum is 50.
The total finding limit is applied before grouping into batches.
.TP
.BI "\-j, \-\-jobs " N
Run at most
.I N
recheck batches concurrently. Must be positive; the default is 1.
All batches inspect the same HEAD snapshot. Completed results are saved and
reported as they arrive, so progress may appear out of batch order.
Failed batches are retried and processing continues by default.
.TP
.B \-\-force
Repeat checks already completed at HEAD with the same harness, model, effort,
and prompt identity.
.TP
.B \-\-dry-run
List planned batches with their finding IDs and, in file mode, file paths,
and show the selected concurrency without invoking the harness or writing state.
.TP
.B \-\-retry-on-error
Automatically retry failed model batches. Enabled by default; use
.B \-\-retry-on-error=false
to disable. Each retry uses the same findings and HEAD, starts a fresh harness
invocation with its own timeout, and counts toward the concurrency cap.
Errors and retry numbers are printed as they occur.
.TP
.BI "\-\-retry-limit " N
Retry each failed batch at most
.I N
times after its initial attempt. The default is 3, meaning at most four attempts
per batch. Zero disables retries; negative values are invalid.
Only a successful attempt is recorded, with its own token usage, cost, and
duration. Cancellation and database errors are not retried.
.TP
.B \-\-continue-on-error
Keep launching batches after retries are exhausted. Enabled by default; the
command processes all selected findings and returns nonzero if any batches
still failed. Use
.B \-\-continue-on-error=false
to stop launching new batches after an exhausted failure. Already running
batches finish their attempts and successful results are saved.
Cancellation or a database error stops running work; completed database
transactions are retained.
.TP
.B "Review options"
The common review options are also accepted. The selected timeout applies to
each batch.
.RE
.TP
.BR "air findings" " [\-\-all]"
Open the interactive findings browser. It defaults to open findings; use
.B \-\-all
to start with every disposition. An interactive terminal is required. See
.B FINDINGS BROWSER
for keys.
.TP
.BI "air finding " FINDING_ID
Show one finding and its complete event history.
.TP
.BR "air finding list" " [" OPTIONS "]"
List findings without opening the interactive browser.
.RS
.TP
.B \-\-all
Include every disposition; shorthand for
.BR "\-\-status all" .
.TP
.BI "\-\-status " STATUS
Filter by
.BR open ,
.BR dismissed ,
.BR resolved ,
or
.BR all .
The default is
.BR open .
.TP
.BI "\-\-severity " SEVERITY
Filter by
.BR error ,
.BR warning ,
.BR info ,
or
.BR all .
The default is
.BR all .
.TP
.BI "\-\-sort " SORT
Sort by
.BR id ,
.BR age ,
.BR file ,
.BR author ,
.BR severity ,
.BR status ,
or
.BR title .
The default is
.BR id .
.TP
.BI "\-\-limit " N
Return at most
.I N
findings. Zero means unlimited.
.TP
.B \-\-json
Write the selected full findings and review attribution as JSON.
.RE
.TP
.BI "air finding dismiss \-\-reason " TEXT " " FINDING_ID
Dismiss an open finding and record the required reason in its history.
.TP
.BI "air finding reopen " FINDING_ID
Return a dismissed or resolved finding to open.
.TP
.BI "air finding note " FINDING_ID " " TEXT
Append a timestamped note to a finding's history.
.TP
.BI "air finding diff " FINDING_ID
Open the finding's introducing commit with
.BR "git difftool" .
.TP
.BI "air finding open " FINDING_ID
Open the current working-tree file at the recorded line using the editor from
.BR "git var GIT_EDITOR" .
.SS History and reports
.TP
.B air log
List reviewed and skipped commits in AIR's stored log.
.TP
.BI "air show [" OPTIONS "] " COMMIT
Show the current review for one processed commit.
.RS
.TP
.B \-\-reviews
List all retained review attempts.
.TP
.BI "\-\-review " N
Show retained review attempt
.IR N .
.TP
.B \-\-json
Write the selected review data as JSON.
.RE
.TP
.BR "air stats" " [\-\-model " MODEL "] [\-\-since " DATE "]"
Summarize token usage, estimated cost, commit-review timing, retained review
and recheck attempts, and current finding counts. Superseded attempts remain
included. The date may be YYYY-MM-DD or RFC3339.
.TP
.BR "air cost" " [\-\-model " MODEL "] [\-\-since " DATE "]"
Show the accounting-focused summary, with attempts grouped by harness, model,
and effort. Unknown prices and token categories not reported by a harness
remain explicit.
.TP
.BR "air export \-\-format " FORMAT " [\-o " FILE "]"
Write a findings report. The format must be
.BR json ,
.BR sarif ,
or
.BR html .
By default the report is written to standard output;
.BI "\-o " FILE
or
.BI "\-\-output " FILE
writes it directly to a file. Use
.B -
for standard output.
JSON and SARIF include current open findings. HTML is one self-contained,
offline, read-only viewer containing every disposition, search and filters,
sorting, details, history, attribution, and bounded introducing-diff excerpts.
.SS Configuration and maintenance
.TP
.B air prompt list
List prompt kinds, sources, and identities.
.TP
.BR "air prompt show" " [\-\-full] " KIND
Show the editable instructions for prompt
.IR KIND .
With
.BR \-\-full ,
also show active project hints and AIR's fixed protocol, safety constraints,
and response contract.
The supported kinds are
.B review
and
.BR recheck .
.TP
.BI "air prompt set \-\-file " PATH " " KIND
Store repository-specific editable instructions read from a UTF-8 file.
.TP
.BI "air prompt set \-\-stdin " KIND
Store repository-specific editable instructions read from standard input.
AIR keeps the fixed protocol and response contract unchanged.
.TP
.BI "air prompt reset " KIND
Remove the repository override and restore the built-in instructions.
Project hints are separate and are not removed by resetting a prompt.
.TP
.BI "air hint add " TEXT
Save temporary project instructions in the repository database and print a
stable numeric ID. Quote multiword text. Each hint must be nonempty UTF-8,
at most 16 KiB; combined active and one-off hint text is limited to 256 KiB.
.TP
.BR "air hint list" " [\-\-prompt IDENTITY]"
List active project hints in ID order. With
.BR \-\-prompt ,
show the immutable hint snapshot for a recorded
.B hints:sha256:
prompt identity instead. Snapshots include one-off hints.
.TP
.BI "air hint remove " HINT_ID
Remove an active hint. IDs are not reused, and hint text used by previous
successful reviews and rechecks is retained in their snapshots.
.PP
Hints supplement built-in or custom prompts for all harnesses. They cannot
override AIR's fixed protocol, and excluding a problem from reporting is not
evidence that an existing finding is resolved. Use finding dismissal for that.
Each invocation freezes its hints for all commits, parallel batches, and retries.
Changes affect future invocations, not already running work. They do not cause
scan to repeat processed commits; use rescan explicitly. Recheck identity
includes hints, so a changed hint set makes open findings eligible again.
Use air prompt show \-\-full review to inspect saved hints in the effective prompt,
and air show (including \-\-review N or \-\-json) to inspect hints used by a review.
Precheck remains non-persistent; its text and JSON reports include the hints used.
Backups include active hints and retained snapshots. No schema upgrade is needed.
.TP
.BI "air config get [\-\-effective] " NAME
Print one database setting. With
.BR \-\-effective ,
print the winning value and its source after applying precedence.
.TP
.BI "air config set [\-\-stdin] " NAME " [" VALUE "]"
Store one repository setting. Use
.B \-\-stdin
to read the value from standard input.
.TP
.BI "air config unset " NAME
Remove one stored repository setting.
.TP
.BR "air config list" " [\-\-effective]"
List stored settings. With
.BR \-\-effective ,
include overrides, defaults, and value sources.
.TP
.B air model list
List known models and whether each has pricing.
.TP
.BI "air model show " NAME
Show one model's pricing details.
.TP
.BI "air model set-pricing [" OPTIONS "] " NAME
Store short- and long-context token prices in USD per million tokens. All
eight price categories are required:
.BR \-\-short-input ,
.BR \-\-short-cached-input ,
.BR \-\-short-cache-write ,
.BR \-\-short-output ,
.BR \-\-long-input ,
.BR \-\-long-cached-input ,
.BR \-\-long-cache-write ,
and
.BR \-\-long-output .
.RS
.TP
.BI "\-\-service-tier " TIER
Set the service tier. The default is
.BR standard .
.TP
.BI "\-\-source " TEXT
Record the pricing source. The default is
.BR manual .
.TP
.BI "\-\-as-of " DATE
Record the pricing date. The default is today.
.TP
.BI "\-\-long-context-threshold " N
Use long-context rates above
.I N
input tokens. The default is 272000.
.RE
.TP
.BI "air model mark-pricing-unknown " NAME
Explicitly record that the model's pricing is unknown.
.TP
.B air db path
Print the AIR database path for the current Git repository. This works before
initialization.
.TP
.BR "air backup" " [" PATH "]"
Create a consistent, private SQLite backup. With no path, AIR creates
.B air-backup-YYYYMMDD-HHMMSS.sqlite
in the current directory and adds a numeric suffix if necessary. The online
backup includes committed WAL state, is integrity-checked, uses mode 0600, and
never overwrites an existing file.
.TP
.BI "air backup import [\-\-force] " PATH
Validate and import an AIR backup into the current repository. The backup must
use the current AIR schema, pass SQLite integrity and foreign-key checks, and
name a baseline on the first-parent history of local master. AIR leaves the
source file unchanged, verifies a temporary copy, and replaces the repository
database while holding the scan lock. Replacing an existing database requires
confirmation unless
.B \-\-force
is supplied. Importing into an uninitialized repository does not prompt.
.TP
.BR "air reset" " [\-\-force]"
Delete all AIR state for the repository, including reviews and configuration.
AIR displays the exact state directory and asks for confirmation unless
.B \-\-force
is supplied.
.SH REVIEW OPTIONS
The commands
.BR scan ,
.BR retry ,
.BR rescan ,
.BR precheck ,
and
.B recheck
accept these common overrides:
.TP
.BI "\-\-hint " TEXT
Add a hint for this invocation only. Repeat the flag for multiple hints;
commas within a hint are literal. One-off hints supplement, rather than replace,
the saved hints and do not change the active database configuration.
.TP
.BI "\-\-harness " HARNESS
Select
.BR codex ,
.BR claude ,
or
.BR gemini .
.TP
.BI "\-\-model " MODEL
Set the exact model identifier recorded with the attempt.
.TP
.BI "\-\-effort " EFFORT
Set the reviewer effort recorded with the attempt. The harness must support
the requested value. Gemini has no per-invocation effort control and therefore
requires the sentinel value
.BR default .
.TP
.BI "\-\-codex-bin " PATH
Set the Codex CLI executable.
.TP
.BI "\-\-codex-profile " PROFILE
Set the Codex configuration profile.
.TP
.BI "\-\-codex-timeout " DURATION
Set the Codex per-commit or per-batch timeout. Go duration syntax is accepted,
such as
.BR 20m .
.TP
.BI "\-\-claude-bin " PATH
Set the Claude Code CLI executable.
.TP
.BI "\-\-claude-timeout " DURATION
Set the Claude Code per-commit or per-batch timeout.
.TP
.BI "\-\-gemini-bin " PATH
Set the Gemini CLI executable.
.TP
.BI "\-\-gemini-timeout " DURATION
Set the Gemini per-commit or per-batch timeout.
.SH CONFIGURATION
Review configuration is resolved in this order:
.PP
.RS
command-line flag > environment variable > database > built-in default
.RE
.PP
The persistent database setting names are:
.BR harness ,
.BR model ,
.BR effort ,
.BR codex-bin ,
.BR codex-profile ,
.BR codex-timeout ,
.BR claude-bin ,
.BR claude-timeout ,
.BR gemini-bin ,
and
.BR gemini-timeout .
.PP
The built-in harness is
.BR codex .
The executable defaults are
.BR codex ,
.BR claude ,
and
.BR gemini .
All three timeout defaults are 20 minutes. Model and effort have no built-in
defaults and must be configured or supplied for a review.
.PP
Each harness uses its existing local authentication and configuration. AIR
does not read or copy credentials. Each review runs in an independent,
non-persistent process with AIR's additional read-only constraints.
.SH FINDINGS BROWSER
Within
.BR "air findings" :
.TP
.BR Up , " " Down , " " j , " " k
Move between findings.
.TP
.BR Left , " " Right
Cycle ID, age, file/line, author, severity, status, and title sorting.
.TP
.B /
Search.
.TP
.BR s , " " v
Cycle status and severity filters.
.TP
.BR Ctrl+U , " " Ctrl+D
Scroll long details.
.TP
.B d
Open the introducing commit in the configured Git difftool.
.TP
.B o
Open the recorded file and line in the configured Git editor.
.TP
.B D
Dismiss the selected finding with a required reason.
.TP
.B r
Reopen the finding after confirmation.
.TP
.B n
Add a note.
.TP
.B ?
Show the complete key reference.
.PP
The detail pane includes the description, location, introducing review,
model and effort, event history, and, where terminal size and source data
allow, the relevant introducing diff hunk.
.SH REVIEW AND ACCOUNTING BEHAVIOR
Commits are reviewed oldest to newest. A merge on master is reviewed against
its first parent; commits on merged branches are not individually reviewed.
Comments, string-content changes, translations, localization resources, and
documentation remain available as context but are out of scope for findings.
.PP
AIR stores harness, model, effort, prompt identity, token usage, cost estimate,
elapsed time for successful commit reviews, summary, findings, and raw response
for each retained attempt. Reasoning tokens are part of output tokens and are
not charged twice. Unknown model prices and usage categories a harness does not
report are kept explicit rather than treated as zero.
.PP
Rescanning is conservative and additive: a new review does not silently delete
findings created by an earlier attempt. Rechecking records
.BR resolved ,
.BR still_present ,
or
.BR uncertain ;
only
.B resolved
closes a finding.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B AIR_HARNESS
Review harness: codex, claude, or gemini.
.TP
.B AIR_MODEL
Exact model identifier.
.TP
.B AIR_REASONING_EFFORT
Reviewer effort.
.TP
.B AIR_CODEX_BIN
Codex CLI executable. Default:
.BR codex .
.TP
.B AIR_CODEX_PROFILE
Codex configuration profile.
.TP
.B AIR_CODEX_TIMEOUT
Codex timeout as a positive Go duration. Default:
.BR 20m .
.TP
.B AIR_CLAUDE_BIN
Claude Code CLI executable. Default:
.BR claude .
.TP
.B AIR_CLAUDE_TIMEOUT
Claude Code timeout as a positive Go duration. Default:
.BR 20m .
.TP
.B AIR_GEMINI_BIN
Gemini CLI executable. Default:
.BR gemini .
.TP
.B AIR_GEMINI_TIMEOUT
Gemini timeout as a positive Go duration. Default:
.BR 20m .
.SH FILES
.TP
.I <git-common-dir>/air/reviews.sqlite
Repository database. It is shared by linked worktrees.
.TP
.I <git-common-dir>/air/scan.lock
Lock preventing concurrent scans and other conflicting operations.
.TP
.I <git-common-dir>/air/
Private repository state directory. It does not modify tracked files.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
The command completed successfully.
.TP
.B 1
The command failed, configuration or arguments were invalid, or a scan batch
recorded one or more review failures. Unless
.B \-\-stop-on-error
was used, a failed scan may still have successfully processed later commits.
A precheck also returns 1 when its
.B \-\-fail-on
threshold matches an outstanding provisional finding.
.SH EXAMPLES
Initialize at a release and configure Codex:
.PP
.EX
air init v1.0.0
air config set model gpt-5.6-luna
air config set effort high
air doctor
air scan --limit 10
.EE
.PP
Review with another harness for one invocation:
.PP
.EX
air scan --harness claude --model claude-model --effort high
air scan --harness gemini --model gemini-model --effort default
.EE
.PP
Review work before pushing without changing AIR state:
.PP
.EX
air precheck --fail-on warning
air precheck --staged --fail-on warning
.EE
.PP
Retry failures and inspect findings:
.PP
.EX
air failures
air retry --continue-on-error
air finding list --all --sort file
air findings
.EE
.PP
Export a shareable report and back up the database:
.PP
.EX
air export --format html -o air-findings.html
air backup
air backup import air-backup-20260831-120000.sqlite
.EE
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR git (1),
.BR git-difftool (1),
.BR sqlite3 (1)
.PP
The project README and complete design are available in the source tree as
.B README.md
and
.BR docs/initial_spec.md .
